    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only JUnit test class; `AcceptanceBase` and `AuditLogCapture` are helpers).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event while keeping each responsibility in its own small unit.\n\n**What was added**\n\n1. **`Owner.getPrimaryIdentifier()`** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 a `@Transient` accessor that returns the owner's *current* primary identifier, today delegating to `getCustomerCode()`. This is the single place that defines \"the owner's primary identifier,\" so when the customer code is later unified into the member id, only this method changes and every consumer (the audit event included) follows automatically.\n\n2. **`OwnerCreatedEvent`** (`rest/audit/OwnerCreatedEvent.java`) \u2014 a new immutable `record` modeling the event, with components declared in the spec's order (`seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event`) and a `TYPE = \"OWNER_CREATED\"` constant. Being a record, the event is immutable by construction.\n\n3. **`OwnerAuditLogger.logCreated`** (`rest/audit/OwnerAuditLogger.java`) \u2014 after the existing human-readable line, it now also builds an `OwnerCreatedEvent` and emits it as JSON. A single `AtomicLong sequence` field on this singleton component supplies the monotonically increasing `seq` across all creates, and the identifier value is sourced from `owner.getPrimaryIdentifier()` (not hardcoded to `customerCode`). Serialization uses the project's Jackson 3 (`tools.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper`), and the JSON is passed as an SLF4J `{}` parameter so its braces aren't misread as placeholders.\n\n**Emitted event** (verified in the test run):\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nThe controller flow was untouched \u2014 it already calls `ownerAuditLogger.logCreated(owner)` after the id is assigned, so the event correctly carries `ownerId`. `./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\nI reused the existing `getMembershipLevel()`, the primary-identifier accessor, and the existing audit logger rather than duplicating any logic, and didn't let the logger accumulate unrelated concerns (the counter is a cohesive part of event emission; the event shape lives in its own record).",
